    "why": "#503: `lmm search --sort` makes the NexusMods search send a `sort: [ModsSort!]` variable and select the Mod type's downloads and endorsements. This recording is what the offline contract test (sort_contract_test.go) checks those names and types against; NO test may ever call the live API. Re-record by hand, from the queries above, when the schema is next known to have moved.",
    "keys": "modsSort = ModsSort; baseSort = BaseSortValue; direction = SortDirection; modFields = the Mod fields the search query selects (Mod.modId/name/summary/version/updatedAt/uploader/downloads/endorsements), each as introspected, so a block's \"type\" is the field's own type; modsSortArg = the `sort` argument of the `mods` query, which must be a list of non-null ModsSort."
